mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course provides a brief introduction to spore plants, gymnosperms, and the classification principles of plants, with a focus on angiosperms. It selects 24 families of medicinal plants with relatively concentrated species, detailing their main morphological characteristics and representative medicinal plants. The aim is to enable students to gain a basic understanding of the plant classification framework based on recognizing a certain number of plant species and to learn fundamental methods for identifying original plants used in traditional Chinese medicine.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
